class Solution {
    public int getLastMoment(int n, int left[], int right[]) {
        int max = 0;
        
        for(int i=0; i<left.length; i++)
            max = Math.max(max, left[i]);
            
        for(int i=0; i<right.length; i++){
            max = Math.max(max, n - right[i]);
        }
        return max;
    }
}
/*
When two ants collide and turn around, it’s equivalent to them passing through each other if ants are indistinguishable.
So instead of simulating collisions, we can:
Treat every ant as moving straight until it falls off the plank.

Plank length = n
Ants in left[] move left, so the time they take to fall = their position itself.
Ants in right[] move right, so the time they take to fall = n - position.
We just need the maximum time among all ants.
*/
